---
/** CLI output preview — matches tsforge terminal event style, not a notebook UI. */
---

<section class="tf-cli-preview" aria-label="Example tsforge session output">
  <h2 class="tf-cli-preview__heading">What a turn looks like</h2>
  <p class="tf-cli-preview__lede">
    The CLI prints tool calls and gate results as they land. Labels below match what you see
    in the terminal.
  </p>

  <div class="tf-cli-preview__terminal">
    <pre class="tf-cli-preview__block" aria-hidden="true"><span class="tf-cli-dim">┌─ </span><span class="tf-cli-accent">✎ edit auth.service.ts</span><span class="tf-cli-dim"> ─────────────────────────</span>
<span class="tf-cli-dim">│ </span><span class="tf-cli-red">- return user as any;</span>
<span class="tf-cli-dim">│ </span><span class="tf-cli-green">+ return user satisfies IUser;</span>
<span class="tf-cli-dim">└────────────────────────────────────────────</span>

<span class="tf-cli-dim">┌─ </span><span class="tf-cli-accent">→ gate (exit 0)</span><span class="tf-cli-dim"> ───────────────────────────────</span>
<span class="tf-cli-dim">│ </span><span class="tf-cli-green">✓ tsc --noEmit</span>
<span class="tf-cli-dim">│ </span><span class="tf-cli-green">✓ strict ESLint (tsforge)</span>
<span class="tf-cli-dim">└────────────────────────────────────────────</span>

<span class="tf-cli-green">  ✓ Gate passed. Checkpoint saved.</span>

<span class="tf-cli-dim">  ⎯ qwen3.6-27b · ctx ~12k/33k 36% · 2 turns · 8s · done · entire workspace</span></pre>
  </div>
</section>
